#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Browser-based live preview server for a LaTeX document.

Generated by the `latex_serve_web` Bazel rule. Don't edit by hand;
edit //latex/private:serve_web.py.tpl instead.

What this is:

* A tiny HTTP server (Python stdlib's http.server) running on
  localhost.
* GET /          -> a single-page HTML wrapper that loads PDF.js from
                    a CDN, renders the current PDF in a canvas, and
                    listens for reload events on /events.
* GET /pdf       -> serves the bytes of bazel-bin/<doc>.pdf.
* GET /events    -> Server-Sent Events stream; emits 'data: reload\\n\\n'
                    every time a rebuild finishes successfully.
* GET /status    -> JSON status of the last build (success, elapsed,
                    timestamp). Used by the page to display compile
                    state ("building...", "✓ built in 0.4s").

Background thread polls the watched source files at POLL_INTERVAL_MS
intervals and runs `bazel build` on every detected change. On
success it bumps a counter and pings every connected SSE listener
(and pushes the new chunk manifest + missing chunks to every
connected WebSocket).

No third-party Python deps. PDF.js is vendored under @rules_latex_pdfjs
and served from /_pdfjs/pdf.mjs at preview time — works fully offline.
"""

